# Verification before completion

Own the final check of the changed user-visible path and the evidence reported before completion or commit. When `test-driven-development` applies, it owns the regression-test choice and red/green sequence; this skill does not require adding a test or repeating that sequence.

Choose the narrowest check that exercises the behavior that could fail. For a UI, CLI, or integration change, smoke-test the actual surface; tests alone do not prove the user-facing path works. Read the exit status and output.

Report only checks actually run and what they proved. Separate untested paths and environmental blockers from verified behavior. Do not claim success from an edit, a test name, an agent report, or an inferred default.
